{
  "requirement": "The `trust-but-verify` crate's `outline` module provides language selection,\nsource outlining, selector resolution, and source structural hashes.\nApplications can use these operations directly on files and supplied source\nsnapshots.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement `requirements.sdk.outlines.independent` has four obligations. The `outline` module must provide language selection, source outlining, selector resolution and structural hashes. Applications must be able to use these directly on files and on supplied source snapshots. The three marked tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs` cover each of them. They import everything from `trust_but_verify::outline`, so they exercise the module as an application would.\n\n- **Language selection**\n  - `fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` checks every bundled language. For each one it checks the name, the claimed extensions and the fingerprint scheme.\n  - It infers the language from an upper-cased extension with `OutlineContent::from_source`. It also selects a language explicitly with `from_source_with`. The two give equal fingerprints.\n  - It asserts that `PlainText` has no extensions.\n  - `fn[file_constructors_infer_the_language_and_return_addressed_contents]` infers Rust from the path `AUTH.RS` and asserts the scheme `rust-structural-v1`.\n- **Source outlining**\n  - The bundled-languages test checks that the root item has selector `\"\"` and spans the whole source. It also checks that every item's span lies within the source.\n  - The file-constructors test asserts the exact selector list `[\"\", \"fn[check_token]\"]`.\n  - `fn[selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits]` checks the item count for an unknown-extension file.\n- **Selector resolution**\n  - `select` is exercised with language-specific selectors such as `fn[check]` and `table[check]`.\n  - `from_id` is exercised with an `OutlineId`, and the selected text is asserted.\n  - The retained-content test selects the root with `\"\"` after the file is edited and still gets the original text.\n- **Structural hashes**\n  - Fingerprints are compared across the file path and supplied-source routes, and across inferred and explicit languages.\n  - The selected-contents test asserts `structural_hash()` equals `fingerprint().value`.\n- **Files and supplied snapshots**\n  - The file-constructors test uses `from_path` and `from_id` for files, and `from_source` for a supplied snapshot, and asserts that the root fingerprints are equal.\n  - The selected-contents test mutates the file after construction. It checks that the snapshot's fingerprint and text are unchanged, and that a fresh `from_id` now fails.\n\nOther tests in the same file add checks outside this requirement, for example unknown-extension line items. I found no plausible violation of the requirement that these tests would miss, and the requirement has no acknowledged gaps.",
  "references": "78ca978244e2c786214b03a4a7b5167bf3ee1e90e18026fc67d7299357660038",
